Potential signed/unsigned narrowing: `pl->num_entries` is likely `int`, but `mp_rand_in_range32` takes `uint32_t`. If `num_entries` can exceed `UINT32_MAX` or be negative (corrupted state), implicit conversion can wrap and lead to OOB access. Consider casting with validation (and early-return if `num_entries <= 1`) to keep bounds safe.

```suggestion
        if (pl->num_entries <= 1)
            return;

        uint32_t nn = (uint32_t)pl->num_entries; // consider asserting pl->num_entries > 0
        uint32_t i = (uint32_t)n;
        size_t j = mp_rand_in_range32(&s, i, nn);
        MPSWAP(struct playlist_entry *, pl->entries[n], pl->entries[j]);
```

